[{"text":"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit[FAD[{k2 + p2, m}, k1 - k2, {k1 - p2, m}]]","anchor":"cb12","section":"Manipulations of FeynAmpDenominators"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{\\left(-2 (\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{k2})+\\text{k1}^2+\\text{k2}^2\\right) \\left(-2 (\\text{k1}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{k1}^2-m^2+\\text{p2}^2\\right) \\left(2 (\\text{k2}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{k2}^2-m^2+\\text{p2}^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"Manipulations of FeynAmpDenominators"},{"text":"1-loop tensor reduction using Passarino-Veltman method is handled by TID","anchor":"one-loop-tensor-reduction","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"FVD[q, \\[Mu]] FVD[q, \\[Nu]] FAD[{q, m}] TID[%, q]","anchor":"cb13","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{q^{\\mu } q^{\\nu }}{q^2-m^2}\\]","anchor":"cb13-2","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{m^2 g^{\\mu \\nu }}{D \\left(q^2-m^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb13-2","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"int = FVD[q, \\[Mu]] SPD[q, p] FAD[{q, m0}, {q + p, m1}] TID[%, q]","anchor":"cb14","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{q^{\\mu } (p\\cdot q)}{\\left(q^2-\\text{m0}^2\\right).\\left((p+q)^2-\\text{m1}^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb14-2","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{p^{\\mu } \\left(\\text{m0}^2-\\text{m1}^2+p^2\\right)^2}{4 p^2 \\left(q^2-\\text{m0}^2\\right).\\left((q-p)^2-\\text{m1}^2\\right)}-\\frac{p^{\\mu } \\left(\\text{m0}^2-\\text{m1}^2+p^2\\right)}{4 p^2 \\left(q^2-\\text{m0}^2\\right)}+\\frac{p^{\\mu } \\left(\\text{m0}^2-\\text{m1}^2+3 p^2\\right)}{4 p^2 \\left(q^2-\\text{m1}^2\\right)}\\]","anchor":"cb14-2","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"By default, TID tries to reduce everything to scalar integrals with unit denominators. However, if it encounters zero Gram determinants, it automatically switches to the coefficient functions","anchor":"cb14-2","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"FCClearScalarProducts[] SPD[p, p] = 0;","anchor":"cb15","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"TID[int, q]","anchor":"cb16","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{p^{\\mu }}{2 \\left(q^2-\\text{m1}^2\\right)}-\\frac{1}{2} i \\pi ^2 \\left(\\text{m0}^2-\\text{m1}^2\\right) p^{\\mu } \\;\\text{B}_1\\left(0,\\text{m0}^2,\\text{m1}^2\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"If we want the result to be express entirely in terms of Passarino-Veltman function, i. e. without FADs, we can use ToPaVe","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"TID[int, q, ToPaVe -> True]","anchor":"cb17","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{1}{2} i \\pi ^2 p^{\\mu } \\;\\text{A}_0\\left(\\text{m1}^2\\right)-\\frac{1}{2} i \\pi ^2 \\left(\\text{m0}^2-\\text{m1}^2\\right) p^{\\mu } \\;\\text{B}_1\\left(0,\\text{m0}^2,\\text{m1}^2\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb17-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"ToPaVe is actually also a standalone function, so it can be used independently of TID","anchor":"cb17-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"FCClearScalarProducts[] FAD[q, {q + p1}, {q + p2}] ToPaVe[%, q]","anchor":"cb18","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\frac{1}{q^2.(\\text{p1}+q)^2.(\\text{p2}+q)^2}","anchor":"cb18-3","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[i \\pi ^2 \\;\\text{C}_0\\left(\\text{p1}^2,\\text{p2}^2,\\text{p1}^2-2 (\\text{p1}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{p2}^2,0,0,0\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb18-3","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"Even if there are no Gram determinants, for some tensor integrals the full result in terms of scalar integrals is just too large","anchor":"cb18-3","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"int = FVD[q, \\[Mu]] FVD[q, \\[Nu]] FAD[q, {q + p1}, {q + p2}] res = TID[int, q];","anchor":"cb19","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[\\frac{q^{\\mu } q^{\\nu }}{q^2.(\\text{p1}+q)^2.(\\text{p2}+q)^2}\\]","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"res // Short","anchor":"cb20","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle }{4 (2-D)\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle \\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle ^2\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle \\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle \\left(\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle ^2-\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle \\right)^2}-\\frac{\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle }{\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle }+\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle -\\frac{\\langle\\langle 44\\rangle\\rangle +\\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle }{4 \\langle\\langle 3\\rangle\\rangle \\langle\\langle 1\\rangle\\rangle ^2}\\]","anchor":"cb20-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"Of course we collect with respect to FAD and isolate the prefactors, but the full result still remains messy","anchor":"cb20-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"Collect2[res, FeynAmpDenominator, IsolateNames -> KK]","anchor":"cb21","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[-\\frac{\\text{KK}(864)}{4 q^2.(-\\text{p1}+\\text{p2}+q)^2}+\\frac{\\text{KK}(868)}{4 q^2.(q-\\text{p1})^2.(q-\\text{p2})^2}-\\frac{\\text{KK}(866)}{4 q^2.(q-\\text{p1})^2}+-\\frac{\\text{KK}(861)}{4 q^2.(q-\\text{p2})^2}\\]","anchor":"cb21-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"In such cases, we can get a much more compact results , if we stick to coefficient functions and do not demand the full reduction to scalars. To do so, use the option UsePaVeBasis","anchor":"cb21-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"res = TID[int, q, UsePaVeBasis -> True]","anchor":"cb22","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"\\[i \\pi ^2 g^{\\mu \\nu } \\;\\text{C}_{00}\\left(\\text{p1}^2,\\text{p2}^2,-2 (\\text{p1}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{p1}^2+\\text{p2}^2,0,0,0\\right)+i \\pi ^2 \\;\\text{p1}^{\\mu } \\;\\text{p1}^{\\nu } \\;\\text{C}_{11}\\left(\\text{p1}^2,-2 (\\text{p1}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{p1}^2+\\text{p2}^2,\\text{p2}^2,0,0,0\\right)+i \\pi ^2 \\;\\text{p2}^{\\mu } \\;\\text{p2}^{\\nu } \\;\\text{C}_{11}\\left(\\text{p2}^2,-2 (\\text{p1}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{p1}^2+\\text{p2}^2,\\text{p1}^2,0,0,0\\right)+i \\pi ^2 \\left(\\text{p1}^{\\nu } \\;\\text{p2}^{\\mu }+\\text{p1}^{\\mu } \\;\\text{p2}^{\\nu }\\right) \\;\\text{C}_{12}\\left(\\text{p1}^2,-2 (\\text{p1}\\cdot \\;\\text{p2})+\\text{p1}^2+\\text{p2}^2,\\text{p2}^2,0,0,0\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb22-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"},{"text":"The resulting coefficient functions can be further reduced with PaVeReduce","anchor":"cb22-1","section":"One-loop tensor reduction"}]